# Framework source repository

This repository declares `repository_kind: framework_source` in
`.ai-team/project-profile.yaml`. It **fabricates** the framework; it is **not**
an installed client project.

## Edit here (product / framework code)

- `src/governed_ai/` — Core runtime source
- `adapters/cursor/` — Cursor adapter source
- `.ai-team/constitution/`, `.ai-team/contracts/`, `.ai-team/schemas/`
- `.cursor/` — live Cursor config for framework development
- `scripts/`, `tools/`, `distribution/`, `tests/` (framework tests)

## Do not treat as product code

- `tests/fixtures/projects/clean/` and `legacy/` — **witness installed projects**
  for migration/distribution tests only. Never edit them to change framework
  behavior; regenerate with `python tests/generate_witness_projects.py --write`.
- Do **not** create `.ai-team/runtime/` or `.ai-team/installation-record.json`
  at the repository root.

## Manifests

| File | Role on this repo |
|---|---|
| `.ai-team/framework-version.json` | Source manifest (paths under `src/`, `adapters/`, …) |
| `.ai-team/installation-record.json` | **Must not exist** here (installed targets only) |

After changing the installable payload, run:

```bash
python scripts/ai-team/sync_source_manifest.py
python scripts/ai-team/validate.py
```

## Forbidden operations

- `python tools/install.py --target .` on this repository (or any
  `framework_source` target)
- Copying runtime files into `.ai-team/runtime/` at the repo root
- Editing witness fixtures instead of `src/` or `adapters/`

Governance metadata (Work Units, gates in `project-state.yaml`) tracks
**framework renovation**, not a post-install client lifecycle.
